(3415, 1, '31.160.50.218', 'POST', '/tickets/97', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '2026-07-14 06:29:37', '{\"opdrachtgever_naam\":\"ACA\",\"afdeling_id\":\"\",\"titel\":\"XDR: #127035498 Windows Multiple Users Failed to Authenticate using Kerberos\",\"omschrijving\":\"Beste Klant,\\r\\n\\r\\nEr is een update betreffende de case CAS-109742-N0B0K7 met als onderwerp \\\" XDR: #127035498 Windows Multiple Users Failed to Authenticate using Kerberos \\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nUpdate:\\r\\n\\r\\nFrank proberen te bellen na onderzoek en hierin is gebleken dat de laptop \\\"LAPTOP-GUH28OEJ\\\" veel meldingen veroorzaakt. Ons advies is om deze opnieuw in te spoelen, want de laptop probeert het Kerberos protocol te authenticeren vanuit veel verschillende (niet verklaarbare) poorten.\\r\\n\\r\\nMocht je op- of aanmerkingen hebben op deze case dan kan je dat melden via een reply op deze mail.\\r\\n\\r\\nAangemaakte case:\\r\\n\\r\\nOp 10-7-2026 10:43 hebben wij deze case geregistreerd en deze heeft onze prioriteit  P3 gekregen. De case is bij ons aangemeld via: Portal\\r\\n\\r\\nDe originele beschrijving van deze case:\\r\\n\\r\\nField Value\\r\\nId 127035498\\r\\nSubject Barracuda XDR - Windows Multiple Users Failed to Authenticate using Kerberos\\r\\nType Alert\\r\\nImpact Medium\\r\\nStatus Open\\r\\nAccount VHE\\r\\nMITRE ATT&CK® Tactic Credential Access\\r\\nMITRE ATT&CK® Technique Brute Force\\r\\nCreated Time 7\\/9\\/2026, 11:57 AM GMT+2\\r\\nSource IP 10.32.23.14\\r\\nSOC Analyst Barracuda XDR SOC\\r\\n\\r\\nDescription\\r\\n\\r\\nIncident Name: Windows Multiple Users Failed to Authenticate using Kerberos\\r\\nOrganization Name: VHE\\r\\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access (TA0006), Brute Force (T1110), Password Spraying (T1110.004)\\r\\nRisk: Medium\\r\\nTicket #: 127035498\\r\\nTime the incident occurred: Thursday July 09 2026, 09:55 AM UTC\\r\\nData Source:\\r\\nClick HERE to respond to this alert in the XDR Dashboard.\\r\\n\\r\\n________________________________\\r\\n\\r\\nWhat is the Threat:\\r\\nBarracuda XDR SOC has identified suspicious password spray activity that indicates a scenario where there are failed logins from one source to one or more destinations against many distinct usernames within 15 minutes. A password spraying is an attack that attempts to access a large number of accounts (usernames) with a few commonly used passwords or testing a singular account (username) with commonly used passwords across multiple destination hosts. In a password spray attack, automated software is used to generate a large number of consecutive guesses as to the value of the desired data. Please see below for further breakdown of the activity.\\r\\n\\r\\nSource IP: 10.32.23.14\\r\\nEvent Start Time: 2026-07-09 09:30:00\\r\\nEvent End Time: 2026-07-09 09:45:00\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following workstations represent the top 3 with the highest number of login attempts:\\r\\n\\r\\nTotal Event Count: 74\\r\\nUnique Event Count: 5\\r\\n\\r\\n________________________________\\r\\n\\r\\nSample Log Event(s):\\r\\n\\r\\n4771001433900x8010000000000000129830039SecurityDC03.corp.vhe.nlLAPTOP-GUH28OEJ$S-1-5-21-1645522239-1580436667-1801674531-11610krbtgt\\/corp.vhe.nl0x408100100x182::ffff:10.32.23.1456290Kerberos pre-authentication failed.\\r\\n\\r\\nAccount Information:\\r\\nSecurity ID: S-1-5-21-1645522239-1580436667-1801674531-11610\\r\\nAccount Name: LAPTOP-GUH28OEJ$\\r\\n\\r\\nService Information:\\r\\nService Name: krbtgt\\/corp.vhe.nl <https:\\/\\/linkprotect.cudasvc.com\\/url?a=https%3a%2f%2fcorp.vhe.nl&c=E,1,dhugPIwSp40so2Ojaal1LW1B-pk_cPYF-nad0b5PcI_BH85VX7Oe8Ph1jcEOX6D-1vbOfNLY_UIkOP-W9jFtH1bDQqHSSXmCEZ5HsHm7LA63jnFnTNPjsw,,&typo=1&ancr_add=1>\\r\\n\\r\\nNetwork Information:\\r\\nClient Address: ::ffff:10.32.23.14\\r\\nClient Port: 56290\\r\\n\\r\\nAdditional Information:\\r\\nTicket Options: 0x40810010\\r\\nFailure Code: 0x18\\r\\nPre-Authentication Type: 2\\r\\n\\r\\nCertificate Information:\\r\\nCertificate Issuer Name:\\r\\nCertificate Serial Number:\\r\\nCertificate Thumbprint:\\r\\n\\r\\nCertificate information is only provided if a certificate was used for pre-authentication.\\r\\n\\r\\nPre-authentication types, ticket options and failure codes are defined in RFC 4120.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf the ticket was malformed or damaged during transit and could not be decrypted, then many fields in this event might not be present.InformationKerberos Authentication ServiceInfoSecurityMicrosoft Windows security auditing.Audit Failure\\r\\n\\r\\nMet vriendelijke groet,\\r\\n\\r\\nRoel van Zon\\r\\nServicedesk\",\"categorie\":\"SOC\",\"prioriteit\":\"kritiek\",\"impact\":\"Normaal\",\"schatting_minuten\":\"\",\"deadline\":\"\",\"behandelaar_id\":\"\"}'),
